🎯 Why Java Doesn't Support Multiple Inheritance?
Interviewer:

Why?

You:

Because of the Diamond Problem.

      Vehicle
      /    \
 Petrol   Electric
      \   /
    HybridCar

Suppose both parent classes have:

start()

Which start() should HybridCar use?

Ambiguity occurs.

Java avoids this problem.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
🎯 What is Polymorphism?
Interviewer:

Explain polymorphism.

You:

Polymorphism means:

Same action, different behavior.

Food Delivery Example

Payment method:

pay()

Can happen through:

UPI
Card
NetBanking
Wallet

Same method.

Different implementations.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
🎯 Compile Time Polymorphism

(Method Overloading)

bookRide()
bookRide(source,destination)
bookRide(source,destination,coupon)

Same method name.

Different parameters.

Output

Compiler decides.

Therefore:

Compile-Time Polymorphism
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🎯 Runtime Polymorphism

(Method Overriding)

Parent:

class Payment{
   void pay()
}

Child:

class UPI{
   void pay()
}

Runtime:

Payment p = new UPI();
p.pay();

Output:

UPI Payment Successful

Actual object decides.

Hence Runtime Polymorphism.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
🎯 What is Abstraction?
Interviewer:

Explain abstraction.

You:

Abstraction means:

Show only what is necessary and hide complexity.

Food Delivery Example

Customer clicks:

Place Order

Customer doesn't know:

Database Queries
API Calls
Payment Verification
Inventory Checks

Everything is hidden.

Real Life Example

Car Driving

You know:

Brake
Accelerator
Steering

You don't know:

Fuel Injection
Combustion Cycle
Engine Timing

That's abstraction.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
🎯 Difference Between Abstraction and Encapsulation

This is asked a LOT.

Encapsulation

Protecting data.

Example:

private int balance;
Abstraction

Hiding complexity.

Example:

Click Pay Now

User doesn't know internal processing.

One-Line Trick
Encapsulation

Hide DATA.

Abstraction

Hide IMPLEMENTATION.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
🎯 What is Interface?
Interviewer:

What is an interface?

You:

An interface is a contract.

Food Delivery Example

Every payment method must support:

pay()

So we create:

interface Payment{
    void pay();
}

Implementations:

UPI
Card
Wallet

All must provide:

pay()
Real World Example

Think of a charger socket.

Socket = Interface

Different chargers:

Samsung
OnePlus
Realme

All follow the same contract.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
🎯 Abstract Class vs Interface
Easy Interview Answer
Abstract Class

Used when classes share common code.

Example:

Vehicle

Common:

engine
fuel
Interface

Used when classes share behavior.

Example:

Payable

All payment systems can pay.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
🎯 What is Constructor?
Interviewer:

What is a constructor?

You:

Constructor initializes objects.

When object is created:

Customer c = new Customer();

Constructor runs automatically.

Example:

Customer(){
   System.out.println("Customer Created");
}

Output:

Customer Created
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🎯 Constructor vs Method
Constructor	Method
Same name as class	Any name
No return type	Has return type
Runs automatically	Called manually

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
🎯 Overloading vs Overriding

This is almost guaranteed in interviews.

Overloading	Overriding
Same class	Parent-child
Different parameters	Same parameters
Compile Time	Runtime
Fast	Slightly slower
Easy Trick
Overloading
Same Name
Different Inputs
Overriding
Same Name
Same Inputs
Different Behavior

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🎯 What is Dynamic Method Dispatch?
Interviewer:

Explain Dynamic Method Dispatch.

You:
Animal a = new Dog();
a.sound();

Reference:

Animal

Object:

Dog

Output:

Dog Barks

Because JVM looks at the actual object.

This is Dynamic Method Dispatch.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
🎯 Association
Real World

Customer places Order.

Customer ---- Order

Both can exist independently.

Customer can exist without an order.

Order can be stored even if customer logs out.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
🎯 Aggregation
Real World

Restaurant has Employees.

Restaurant ---> Employees

If restaurant closes:

Employees still exist.

Weak relationship.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
🎯 Composition
Real World

Order contains OrderItems.

Order ---> OrderItems

If order is deleted:

Items are deleted too.

Strong relationship.
